                <pb facs="0589" n="1323" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1323"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Apprehension of massacre of missionaries alike at Aleppo, Hadjin, Mersine, and
                    Marash. Missionaries here agree that danger would be greater in transit than to
                    stay calmly at their posts. * * * British ambassador will apply for use of
                    British vessels if needed to take refuge before ours can arrive. British
                    missions all located on the coast. The situation here is still precarious.
                    Orders have issued for all provinces to protect Americans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
